fresh-eyes: independent cold reviewer (subagent, no authorship of this branch), full scope of the two commits carrying the accepted confinement follow-ups.

Verdict LAND on this tip after two rounds.

Round one returned DO-NOT-LAND on one item: four of the twelve climb
guards survived their own removal. present_but_irregular was never
probed, only rename's destination climbed, and remove_dir and
dir_is_empty were probed with a non-empty target, where ENOTEMPTY
stands in for the refusal — the same masking this suite had already
been caught by once.

Round two re-ran the mutation pass independently: 13 of 13 caught.
Twelve single-site guard deletions each die on their own named
assertion with no cascades, and the whole-guard-off mutant fails two
tests. The reviewer established no assertion passes for a wrong
reason: the mutants demonstrate the rename source is otherwise
movable, the climbed path resolves to a real directory, and
docs/hollow is genuinely empty and removable through the climb.

Also proved in round one: whole-component semantics, with
docs/..hidden and notes..md and ..md accepted and every true parent
component refused, and the right split on Windows separators per
platform; the lexical refusal reads as refused_by_confinement while a
mode-000 EACCES reads as a fault; the deleted NotFound tiebreaker
hides nothing, checked against the old bug's exact shape rebuilt with
a symlink; consumer smokes green for tisket (a 0.3.1 to 0.3.3 jump)
and zettel (0.3.0 to 0.3.3); the changelog claim that no consumer
builds a name with '..' verified against all three, which gate caller
text through is_plain_stem before any join; and both new module-doc
paragraphs match measured behaviour.

199 tests with --all-features, clippy clean, fmt clean.
